      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "ComfyUI-WanVideoWrapper",
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Wan-Animate-2\nhttps://github.com/Wan-Video/Wan-Animate-2 — the driving video is used as is, no pose or face extraction needed.\n\n**Models** (`models/diffusion_models`): Wan-Animate-2 14B base or distilled, bf16 / fp8 / **INT8 ConvRot** (ComfyUI format, auto detected with quantization `disabled`, uses INT8 matmul through comfy_kitchen; `int8_dequant` dequantizes on the fly instead). Weights: https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.2-Animate-2-14B\nText encoder `umt5-xxl-enc`, CLIP vision `clip_vision_h`, VAE `Wan2_1_VAE`.\n\n**Settings**\n- Base model: 40 steps, cfg 3.0, shift 5, `log_scale` 0.0\n- Distilled model: 10 steps, cfg 1.0, scheduler `euler`, `log_scale` -1.3\n- Prompt: describe the character's appearance and the background, not the motion (upstream uses a Chinese template: 人物外观描述：... 背景描述：...)\n- Pose branch prompt: upstream default is 人物动作的参考视频, leave `pose_text_embeds` unconnected to reuse the main prompt\n- `uncond_skip_block` 9 matches upstream's CFG pass\n\n**Long videos**: when `num_frames` is larger than `frame_window_size` (81), the video is generated window after window, each continuing from the last frame of the previous one, like upstream. Context options also work.\n\n**Memory**: `pose_cache` keeps the pose branch activations (it never changes during sampling) and roughly halves the time, ~12 GB RAM at 832x480x81 in bf16, `int8` halves that."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
  ],
